1	/**
2	 * doc-links.test.ts — every relative link and anchor between documents resolves.
3	 *
4	 * ## The failure this exists for
5	 *
6	 * `docs/` is about to be split from six flat files into a tree, and the first
7	 * measurement of that split was that ninety-five links run between these documents.
8	 * Roughly half name a file and half name a heading inside one. A move breaks them
9	 * all at once, and a broken link in Markdown is silent: GitHub renders it, it looks
10	 * like a link, and it 404s only for the reader who follows it.
11	 *
12	 * That is exactly the failure the documentation issue was opened for — a document
13	 * that goes stale with nothing saying so — which makes a split performed without
14	 * this test an instance of the disease it is meant to cure.
15	 *
16	 * ## What it does not check
17	 *
18	 * Absolute URLs. A link to `https://github.com/...` may rot, and asking the network
19	 * would make this test slow and flaky in equal measure. Nothing here leaves the
20	 * repository.
21	 *
22	 * Nor does it check that a link is the RIGHT one: a link to an existing heading
23	 * that answers a different question passes. Only that what it names is there.
24	 */
